  "reason": "Fixed: newly registered customers can now be read back through customers.lookup@1. Cause: lookup was reading the legacy CRM's nightly export (src/legacy/crm.mjs). That export is regenerated only once a day, so it never contains customers registered since. customers.register@1 writes to the application's customer store (src/store.mjs), which is the system of record and is filled from the same export at start-up. Change: lookup now reads from the store (getCustomer) and still returns NOT_FOUND when the customer does not exist. Only src/handlers/customers.lookup.mjs changed; no contract was modified. The agent verified the proposal: the contract is unchanged, outputs conform to the schema, only declared failures occur, answers for existing customers are unchanged for customers.lookup@1 and billing.contact@1, and customers.register@1's declared verification (customer-readable, registered-event) confirms.",
